{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "PricePulse Receipt Analysis API",
    "version": "v1",
    "description": "HTTP surface of the PricePulse backend: submit a receipt image for analysis and poll its result.\n\n**Envelope.** Every JSON body carries `envelopeVersion: \"v1\"`. Success bodies carry `status`; failure bodies carry `error`. A body carries `requestId` if and only if the key has already passed edge validation at the point the answer is produced, which is why `UNAUTHORIZED`, `INVALID_REQUEST_ID` and the GET's `RATE_LIMITED` do not have it.\n\n**Idempotency.** `POST` is keyed by `(authenticated user, Idempotency-Key)`. Repeating the call with the same key and the same image bytes returns the current state of the same operation; the same key with different bytes is `409 REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT`.\n\n**The two endpoints differ on status codes, on purpose.** `POST` answers `202` while the operation is still open and `200` once it has reached a terminal state; `GET` answers `200` for any operation it finds, terminal or not.\n\nWritten from the route code (`StartReceiptAnalysisRoute`, `ReceiptAnalysisStatusRoute`) and the two response builders. The `document` schema is embedded from `contracts/receipt-analysis-result.v1.schema.json`, which remains the source of truth: regenerate this file when that one changes."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:8080",
      "description": "Local run"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://{host}",
      "description": "Deployed instance",
      "variables": {
        "host": {
          "default": "pricepulse-backend.up.railway.app",
          "description": "Deployment host. Replace with the real one."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Receipt analyses",
      "description": "Submit and poll receipt analysis operations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Operations",
      "description": "Process-level endpoints."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/v1/receipt-analyses": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Receipt analyses"
        ],
        "summary": "Submit a receipt image for analysis",
        "operationId": "startReceiptAnalysis",
        "description": "Admission runs in a fixed order: authenticate, validate the key, advisory lookup plus layer 1, read and validate the upload, layer 2, then exactly one invocation of the use case.\n\n**Upload limits.** Exactly one part, named `image`, carrying a filename and a declared `Content-Type` of `image/jpeg` or `image/png`. The image part may not exceed 5,242,880 bytes; the whole multipart envelope may not exceed 5,505,024 bytes; header dimensions may not exceed 6000x6000. A declared `Content-Length` may only reject a request early. It never authorises acceptance, which is always decided by counting real bytes.\n\n**Validation order within the upload** is structure, declared MIME, image size, envelope size, dimensions, then integrity, and the first failure wins. Integrity is structural: PNG is checked chunk by chunk with CRC-32, JPEG structurally only, so a structurally valid JPEG whose entropy data is corrupted is accepted.\n\n**Rate limits.** 10 requests per minute in a fixed 60-second window: per `(user, key)` when the operation probably already exists, and per user when it is probably new.",
        "security": [
          {
            "firebaseIdToken": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "Idempotency-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "required": true,
            "description": "Client-generated key, at most 128 characters of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`. Validated at the edge before any store or limiter is touched.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
            },
            "example": "b3f1c2a4-7e9d-4a10-9c33-0f5d6e7a8b91"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "multipart/form-data": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "image"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "image": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "binary",
                    "description": "The receipt image. Must be a file part -- a filename parameter is what makes it one -- named exactly `image`."
                  }
                }
              },
              "encoding": {
                "image": {
                  "contentType": "image/jpeg, image/png"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The operation has reached a terminal state: SUCCEEDED, FAILED or FAILED_NO_PROVIDER.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnalysisEnvelope"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "202": {
            "description": "Accepted, and still open: RECEIVED, PROCESSING or RECONCILING. Poll the GET endpoint.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnalysisEnvelope"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Either the Idempotency-Key failed validation (`INVALID_REQUEST_ID`, no requestId in the body) or the upload was malformed (`MALFORMED_UPLOAD`, with requestId).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InvalidRequestIdError"
                    },
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UploadRejectedError"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Missing, malformed, or rejected bearer token. Indistinguishable across all failure modes by design.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UnauthorizedError"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "WWW-Authenticate": {
                "description": "Always the literal `Bearer`.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "const": "Bearer"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "No grant had spare credit.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InsufficientCreditsError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The key already exists for this user with different image bytes.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ConflictError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "410": {
            "description": "The operation was tombstoned.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GoneError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "413": {
            "description": "`IMAGE_TOO_LARGE`, `REQUEST_TOO_LARGE`, or `IMAGE_DIMENSIONS_TOO_LARGE`.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UploadRejectedError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "415": {
            "description": "`UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` (declared type outside the accepted set) or `MEDIA_TYPE_MISMATCH` (real signature contradicts the declared type, or the file is not intact).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UploadRejectedError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "An admission layer limited the request.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RateLimitedError"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "Retry-After": {
                "description": "Seconds left in the current window; equals the body's `retryAfter`.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "maximum": 60
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Ingestion or the use case failed unexpectedly.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InternalError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/receipt-analyses/{requestId}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Receipt analyses"
        ],
        "summary": "Read the state of a receipt analysis",
        "operationId": "getReceiptAnalysis",
        "description": "Read-only: the single store call is a lookup. Order is authenticate, apply the per-user limit, validate the path, then read, so an unauthenticated caller reaches neither the limiter nor the store.\n\nThe operation is keyed by `(authenticated user, requestId)`, and the user always comes from the verified token, never from the path: another user's key answers `404`, exactly like one that never existed.\n\n**Rate limit.** 30 requests per minute per user, in a fixed 60-second window.",
        "security": [
          {
            "firebaseIdToken": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "requestId",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "description": "The same value sent as `Idempotency-Key` on the POST.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The operation was found. This is `200` for any lifecycle, including the non-terminal ones -- unlike the POST, which answers `202` for those.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnalysisEnvelope"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "The path value failed edge validation.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InvalidRequestIdError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Missing, malformed, or rejected bearer token. Indistinguishable across all failure modes by design.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UnauthorizedError"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "WWW-Authenticate": {
                "description": "Always the literal `Bearer`.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "const": "Bearer"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such operation for this user.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/NotFoundError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "410": {
            "description": "The operation was tombstoned.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GoneError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "The per-user polling limit fired. Answered before the path is validated, so the body carries no requestId.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RateLimitedErrorWithoutRequestId"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "Retry-After": {
                "description": "Seconds left in the current window; equals the body's `retryAfter`.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "integer",
                  "minimum": 0,
                  "maximum": 60
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "The store failed unexpectedly.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InternalError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Operations"
        ],
        "summary": "Liveness probe",
        "operationId": "health",
        "description": "Unauthenticated. Answers `200` with the literal body `OK` as plain text. It does not check the database or any downstream dependency.",
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The process is up.",
            "content": {
              "text/plain": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "const": "OK"
                },
                "example": "OK"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "firebaseIdToken": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "bearerFormat": "JWT",
        "description": "A Firebase ID token. The scheme name is matched case-insensitively and must be followed by exactly one space and a non-blank token."
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "AnalysisEnvelope": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The single success envelope, built by ReceiptAnalysisStatusResponses.found and shared by both endpoints. `document` is present if and only if status is SUCCEEDED; `reason` if and only if status is FAILED_NO_PROVIDER. FAILED deliberately carries no reason: the domain has exactly one cause for it.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "status"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "status": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "RECEIVED",
              "PROCESSING",
              "RECONCILING",
              "SUCCEEDED",
              "FAILED",
              "FAILED_NO_PROVIDER"
            ]
          },
          "document": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReceiptAnalysisResultV1",
            "description": "Only when status is SUCCEEDED."
          },
          "reason": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Only when status is FAILED_NO_PROVIDER.",
            "enum": [
              "REQUEST_CONSTRUCTION_FAILED",
              "PROVIDER_CREDENTIAL_UNAVAILABLE",
              "MALFORMED_REQUEST",
              "AUTHENTICATION_REJECTED",
              "ACCESS_FORBIDDEN",
              "RETRY_EXHAUSTED",
              "BILLING_OR_QUOTA_EXHAUSTED",
              "UNRECOGNIZED_RESPONSE",
              "RESPONSE_FAILED",
              "RESPONSE_CANCELLED",
              "RATE_LIMITED",
              "TRANSIENT_PROVIDER_FAILURE"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "UnauthorizedError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Byte-for-byte identical across all six authentication failure modes; carries no requestId, because it is answered before the key is validated.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "UNAUTHORIZED"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "InvalidRequestIdError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Answered during key validation, so it carries no requestId.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "INVALID_REQUEST_ID"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "NotFoundError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "A requestId belonging to another user is indistinguishable from one that never existed.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "NOT_FOUND"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "GoneError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The operation was tombstoned.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "GONE"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "ConflictError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The key already exists for this user with different image bytes.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "InsufficientCreditsError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "No grant had spare credit.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "InternalError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "The controlled answer to an unexpected store or use-case failure. The body never carries the underlying driver message.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "INTERNAL_ERROR"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "UploadRejectedError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "One body per rejection constant, written literally on the wire so a rename of the Kotlin enum cannot silently change what clients receive.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "MALFORMED_UPLOAD",
              "UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE",
              "IMAGE_TOO_LARGE",
              "REQUEST_TOO_LARGE",
              "IMAGE_DIMENSIONS_TOO_LARGE",
              "MEDIA_TYPE_MISMATCH"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "RateLimitedError": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "POST: both admission layers fire after the Idempotency-Key has been validated, so the body carries the requestId.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "requestId",
          "error",
          "retryAfter"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "requestId": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "RATE_LIMITED"
            ]
          },
          "retryAfter": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 60,
            "description": "Seconds left in the current fixed window. Mirrors the Retry-After header exactly: both come from one captured decision, never a second clock read."
          }
        }
      },
      "RateLimitedErrorWithoutRequestId": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "GET: the per-user layer fires before the path is validated, so no requestId is available to report.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": [
          "envelopeVersion",
          "error",
          "retryAfter"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "envelopeVersion": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "error": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "RATE_LIMITED"
            ]
          },
          "retryAfter": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "maximum": 60,
            "description": "Seconds left in the current fixed window. Mirrors the Retry-After header exactly: both come from one captured decision, never a second clock read."
          }
        }
      },
      "ReceiptAnalysisResultV1": {
        "title": "ReceiptAnalysisResult",
        "description": "Wire representation of the Android domain type com.tonycorreia.pricepulse.domain.receiptanalysis.ReceiptAnalysis, version v1. Represents only the semantic analysis result -- never a transport error, credit/idempotency state, or UI issue/disposition.",
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "schemaVersion",
          "documentStatus",
          "merchantName",
          "purchasedAt",
          "total",
          "items"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "schemaVersion": {
            "const": "v1"
          },
          "documentStatus": {
            "description": "Mirrors ReceiptDocumentStatus.kt exactly -- 4 literals, no fallback/unknown value.",
            "enum": [
              "COMPLETE",
              "PARTIAL",
              "UNREADABLE",
              "NOT_A_RECEIPT"
            ]
          },
          "merchantName": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TextField"
          },
          "purchasedAt": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InstantField"
          },
          "total": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MoneyField"
          },
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReceiptAnalysisItem"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "FieldConfidence": {
        "description": "Mirrors FieldConfidence.kt exactly -- 4 literals.",
        "enum": [
          "HIGH",
          "MEDIUM",
          "LOW",
          "UNKNOWN"
        ]
      },
      "ReceiptAnalysisItem": {
        "description": "Mirrors ReceiptAnalysisItem.kt -- all 5 fields required in the envelope (each may itself be the missing variant).",
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "description",
          "quantity",
          "unit",
          "unitPrice",
          "totalPrice"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "description": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TextField"
          },
          "quantity": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/QuantityField"
          },
          "unit": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TextField"
          },
          "unitPrice": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MoneyField"
          },
          "totalPrice": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MoneyField"
          }
        }
      },
      "TextField": {
        "description": "Wire form of ReceiptField<String> (merchantName, description, unit). Mirrors ReceiptField.kt: Present(value non-blank, confidence) | Invalid(rawDescription) | Missing.",
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "status",
              "value",
              "confidence"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "present"
              },
              "value": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1,
                "pattern": "\\S"
              },
              "confidence": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FieldConfidence"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "status",
              "rawDescription"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "invalid"
              },
              "rawDescription": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "status"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "missing"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "InstantField": {
        "description": "Wire form of ReceiptField<Instant> (purchasedAt). value is ISO-8601 UTC, never a numeric timestamp.",
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "status",
              "value",
              "confidence"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "status": {
                "const": "present"
              },
              "value": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "RFC 3339 date-time restricted to UTC -- must end in 'Z', never a numeric offset like +02:00.",
